===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[Montezuma]][['s]] [[revenge]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|humorous}} [[diarrhea|Diarrhea]] experienced by [[tourist]]s after drinking water or eating food in [[Mexico]] as a result of a [[bacteria]] [[strain]] to which [[native]] Mexicans are [[immune]].
#* {{quote-book|author=John-Claude Guillebaud|author2=John Simmons, transl.|chapter=Montezuma’s Revenge|title=Return to Vietnam|location=London; New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Verso Books}}|year=1994|page=112|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=P2ivbb080lUC&pg=PA112|isbn=978-0-86091-418-1|passage='''Montezuma's Revenge''', everybody knows, is the persistent intestinal illness that spoils the good humour of tourists in the tropics. Could there be a '''Montezuma's Revenge''' of the soul? There could. We caught it.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Jim Foster|chapter=Picking on Senator Going Too Far|title=I Hate to Complain, but&nbsp;…: A Collection of Humorous Something-or-others|location=Toronto, Ont.; Headington, Oxford; Tonawanda, N.Y.|publisher=Hounslow Press, {{w|Dundurn Press}}|year=1999|page=19|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=PY47AgAAQBAJ&pg=PA19|isbn=978-0-88882-214-7|passage=There's a lot of flu bugs floating around. I think it is commendable that he thought enough of his fellow senators to keep his diseases to himself. I don't know what he had, but I suspect it was '''Montezuma's Revenge'''. (Mexico is the only country in th world where the expression "Royal Flush" has nothing to do with playing cards.)}}
#* {{quote-book|author=Jeffrey M. Pilcher|chapter=From “Montezuma’s Revenge” to “Mexican Truffles”: Culinary Tourism across the Rio Grande|editor=Lucy M. Long|title=Culinary Tourism|series=Material Worlds|location=Lexington, Ky.|publisher={{w|University Press of Kentucky}}|year=2004|page=76|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ift27DhC1BAC&pg=PA76|isbn=978-0-8131-2292-2|passage=President {{w|Jimmy Carter}} arrived in Mexico City for a state visit on February 14, 1979, and proceeded to recall for his hosts a previous encounter with Mexican culture, decades earlier as a naval officer, in which he had contracted what he described as "'''Montezuma's revenge'''." This indelicate reference to tourist's diarrhea became something of an international incident; Mexican Preident {{w|José López Portillo}} insisted that his country be treated with respect, while the local press denounced the remark as a "typical Yankee slur."}}
#* {{quote-book|author=George Ann Huck|author2=Jann E. Freed|authorlink2=Jann Freed|chapter=|title=Women of Yucatán: Thirty Who Dare to Change Their World|location=Jefferson, N.C.|publisher={{w|McFarland & Company}}|year=2010|page=18|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=6R-hBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA18|isbn=978-0-7864-4526-4|passage=We warily sipped the lemonade, knowingly flirting with the tourist stomach disorder known here as '''Moctezuma's revenge'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|author=M. I. Lastman|chapter=Answers|title=Rocky Mountain Locust: Opus I, Trio: A Novel|location=Victoria, B.C.|publisher=[[w:Friesens|FriesenPress]]|year=2014|section=part 1 (Jim)|page=32|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=90ktBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA32|isbn=978-1-4602-4797-6|passage=When we were together in Mexico in the early seventies, she came down with a bad case of '''Moctezuma's revenge''', complaining that she'd never been sick to her stomach before.}}

